    "scraped_content": "October 14th: I don't know how much longer I can keep pretending everything is fine. The weight on my chest hasn't lifted in weeks. I look at the people around me and they seem so alive, while I feel like I'm just watching from behind glass. Sleep is impossible again. I stare at the ceiling until 4 AM wondering why I feel so disconnected. \n\nOctober 20th: Tried to go out today. Couldn't make it past the driveway. The anxiety was suffocating. I canceled on Sarah again. She stopped calling. Maybe it's better this way. I don't want to burden anyone with this darkness. \n\nOctober 25th: I feel completely empty. The activities I used to love bring no joy anymore. I wrote a letter to my mom but couldn't send it. What would I even say? Sorry for feeling this way?",
